      "block_id": "s1:block:00921-00942",
      "page_role": "narration",
      "speaker_en": null,
      "jp": "リンシャに部屋へ案内された後、いざという時の為に\n脱出経路等の確認を済ませた俺は漸く部屋に落ち着き\n暫くの間自室となる部屋の中を見渡した\nこの部屋は日当たりも良く清潔感のある良い部屋で、\n二階に当たるこの部屋の窓からは\n街の中央に位置する広場が一望出来る。\n昔、逃亡の日々を送っていた頃によく泊まった安宿とは\n雲泥の差だな……\n不意に俺の脳裏にあの頃の生活が甦る……\nもう何十年も昔だ、俺はある理由から太古の昔に\n天へと消えたと伝えられる一人の女神と戦った\n絶対である筈の力を持つ女神に対して、奇跡的にも\n相打つ形で勝利し、女神の意思を封じた俺は、\n戦いで致命傷を負った俺本来の身体の代わりとして\n其の女神の肉体を奪う事で生き延びた……。\nそれが……全ての始まりだった……",
      "en": "Rinsha showed me to my room. After confirming escape routes and such for emergencies, I finally settled in and looked around the room that would be mine for a while. It's a nice, clean room with good sunlight. From its second-floor window, I can overlook the plaza in the town center. Compared to the cheap inns I used to stay in during my fugitive days, it's like heaven and earth... Suddenly, memories of those days resurface in my mind... It was decades ago. For a certain reason, I fought a goddess who was said to have vanished into the heavens in ancient times. Against a goddess with supposedly absolute power, I miraculously managed to fight her to a draw and seal her will. Then, instead of my own body that suffered fatal wounds in the battle, I survived by seizing that goddess's body... That... was the beginning of everything..."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "s1:block:00944-00959",
      "page_role": "narration",
      "speaker_en": null,
      "jp": "俺が倒した神は、今この世界を治めている神々とは敵対する\n邪神と呼ばれる存在であったが、それでも神である事には\n変わらず、神を倒し其の力を奪った俺を他の神々と其の信徒達\nは『神殺し』と呼び畏れ、俺という存在を消し去ろうとした\nそれから数十年、女神の肉体を得た為に老いる事の無くなった\n俺は、全世界の大半を敵として時には戦い逃げ続けた末、\n数多ある神々のどの派閥にも属さぬ大国レウィニアの唯一神\n『水の巫女』と同盟を結ぶ事で仮初めの安住の地を得た……\nそれから十数年……水の巫女を国教とするレウィニア国内では\n他の神や其の信徒等に命を狙われる事は少なくなった\nだが、レウィニアに属さないこの街で俺の正体が\n知られてしまったとすれば、この街の住人全てが俺の敵となり\nレウィニアに逃げ帰るまで命を狙われ続ける羽目になるだろう",
      "en": "The god I defeated was called an evil god, opposed to the gods who now rule this world. Yet she was still a god. For defeating her and taking her power, the other gods and their followers feared me as the 'God Slayer' and sought to erase my existence. For decades, my body, no longer aging because I had taken the goddess's flesh, I fought and fled from much of the world. At last, I formed an alliance with the Water Maiden, the sole deity of the great nation Revienia—who belongs to no faction among the many gods—and gained a temporary haven. Over ten years have passed since then... In Revienia, where the Water Maiden is the state religion, attacks on my life by other gods or their followers have grown rare. But if my true identity were known in this town, which does not belong to Revienia, all its people would become my enemies, and I would be hunted until I could flee back to Revienia."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "s1:block:00964-00965",
      "page_role": "narration",
      "speaker_en": null,
      "jp": "部屋には荷物を入れる為の鍵付きの箱などが置いてあり、\n長期滞在用の部屋である事が窺える。",
      "en": "The room has a lockable chest for luggage and such, so it's clearly a room for long-term stays."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "s1:block:00970-00976",
      "page_role": "narration",
      "speaker_en": null,
      "jp": "物思いに耽っていた俺は、ふと思い出して、\nベッドの横に置いた荷物の中から鞘に収められた\n一振りの短剣を取り出した。\n大きな飾りこそ無いが、女性を象った滑らかな曲線と\n落ち着いた意匠の施されたその短剣を手にした瞬間、\n俺の頭の中に気怠げな若い女性の声が響く。",
      "en": "Lost in thought, I suddenly remembered, and from the luggage set beside the bed, I took out a single sheathed short sword. It lacked large decorations, but the moment I held that short sword with its smooth, womanly curves and subdued design, a languid young woman's voice echoed in my head."
    }
  ]
}

